WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.016 --> 00:00:05.864
Doctor’s Report: September 29, 1876, London My name is Jack Seward and I am a well-respected doctor

2
00:00:05.865 --> 00:00:14.491
in London, where I have a general practice at the local hospital. I have seen many patients with

3
00:00:14.492 --> 00:00:21.745
rare diseases, but none as shocking as the case of poor Miss Lucy. I was summoned to

4
00:00:21.746 --> 00:00:31.745
Lucy’s seaside home by her mother, who explained that the young woman had fallen ill after being attacked

5
00:00:31.746 --> 00:00:38.729
by a wild dog. I immediately noted that she was unusually pale, as though she had lost

6
00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:46.285
a lot of blood. However, I knew this to be false because she suffered only two small

7
00:00:46.286 --> 00:00:56.950
bites to the side of her neck. I couldn’t come up with a satisfactory diagnosis, so I contacted

8
00:00:56.951 --> 00:01:06.848
my old college chum, Professor Van Helsing, to see if he could provide some help. He told

9
00:01:06.849 --> 00:01:11.491
me to place a ring of garlic around Lucy’s neck and, although I thought this was an

10
00:01:11.492 --> 00:01:19.372
unusual treatment, I followed his directions. For a week, I volunteered to watch over Lucy as she slept.

11
00:01:19.373 --> 00:01:27.387
We moved Lucy from her seaside home to her parents’ London residence so that I could continue

12
00:01:27.388 --> 00:01:32.316
to work at the hospital during the day. This was quite tiring, so one night, I decided to

13
00:01:32.341 --> 00:01:42.305
skip my visit to their home and get some rest in my own bed. I knew that

14
00:01:42.306 --> 00:01:44.964
Lucy’s servants would take good care of her in my absence. The next morning, I found a

15
00:01:45.031 --> 00:01:50.911
letter from Van Helsing that read: "My friend, please watch over Lucy tonight─I believe she is in grave

16
00:01:50.912 --> 00:01:58.379
danger. I will be there tomorrow." But, that was written last night! Oh, no, was I too

17
00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:05.193
late? I rushed off to Lucy’s home to check on her and was surprised to find Van Helsing

18
00:02:05.194 --> 00:02:09.614
already on the porch. "There’s no answer . . . ," he said. "I’ve knocked several times.

19
00:02:09.615 --> 00:02:13.812
Did you not read my letter?" "I’m sorry, professor, but I didn’t receive your letter until this

20
00:02:13.974 --> 00:02:17.783
morning. I think you were right; there is a problem," I explained. "Lucy’s mother left me a key,

21
00:02:17.784 --> 00:02:25.536
so I can let us in." We proceeded through the hall into the kitchen, moving cautiously, and

22
00:02:25.537 --> 00:02:30.370
were shocked to find the servants passed out on the floor. "They’re not dead," I said. "They’re

23
00:02:30.371 --> 00:02:36.767
still breathing." Upstairs, we discovered Lucy and her mother sprawled across the floor of the master bedroom. Van

24
00:02:36.768 --> 00:02:42.275
Helsing leaned down to check the mother’s pulse and shook his head in despair. "She’s dead," he

25
00:02:42.531 --> 00:02:51.856
said solemnly. "All the blood has been drained from her body. But this young woman is still breathing."

26
00:02:51.943 --> 00:02:58.855
The garlic necklace lay in pieces all over the carpet and there was fresh blood dripping from

27
00:02:58.983 --> 00:03:06.257
Lucy’s lips. I wiped it clean while Van Helsing returned to the kitchen to revive the servants

28
00:03:06.324 --> 00:03:11.553
and inform them of the tragedy. He sent one of them to retrieve Arthur from his office, which

29
00:03:11.578 --> 00:03:19.831
was nearby. That night, the three of us kept vigil in Lucy’s room, each taking a turn

30
00:03:19.904 --> 00:03:25.427
watching over her while the other two slept. Van Helsing woke me just as the sun was peeking

31
00:03:25.428 --> 00:03:31.900
over the rooftops of London. "Her wound has healed," he said and pointed to her neck. "She

32
